estigious-international-literary-awards/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d72\"},\"ref\":\"d72\",\"snippet\":\" ... before its nomination to 25,000 copies in the nine months after its win. (Not bad for a 624-page epic about a woman who won't get out of bed.) And the first winner, Han Kang's The Vegetarian in 2016, translated by Deborah Smith, about a ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/jul/29/its-exciting-its-powerful-how-translated-fiction-captured-a-new-generation-of-readers\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d47\"},\"ref\":\"d47\",\"snippet\":\" ... Deborah Smith is the Man Booker International Prize–winning translator of The Vegetarian by Han Kang and other books.\\n\\nHarmless Like You by Rowan Hisayo Buchanan\\n\\nRowan Hisayo Buchanan is a British-Japanese-Chinese-American novelist. She received a BA from Columbia University in New York, and currently ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.aspeninstitute.org/blog-posts/20-new-works-fiction-social-impact/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d73\"},\"ref\":\"d73\",\"snippet\":\" ... And for those of us interested in reading books that originate beyond the English-speaking world, they don't come much more major than the Man Booker International Prize, which was awarded for the first time last year to Han Kang and translator Deborah Smith for The Vegetarian ... \",\"title\":\"https://ayearofreadingtheworld.com/2017/04/29/book-of-the-month-samanta-schweblin/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"6171a0fbd8024501